  "question": {
    "text": "Two radioactive elements <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> initially have same number of atoms. The half life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is same as the average life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> are decay constants of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> respectively, then choose the correct relation from the given options."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is given that&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The half life of a substance is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
  }
